5. Failure Modes and Mitigation Strategies

Failure Mode 1 — Cross-Model Disagreement Explosion. When ensemble outputs exceed the injectivity radius $r = \pi/2$ on $\mathbb{S}^{d-1}$, the Fréchet mean becomes ill-conditioned and CVF-R breaks.
Mitigation: The Semantic Drift Detector halts fusion when $d_{\mathcal{M}}(y_i, y_j) > \pi/4$, routing tasks to human review.

Failure Mode 2 — Routing Misclassification Cascade. Tasks misclassified below the Lemma 0 completeness threshold pollute the performance registry.
Mitigation: The Completeness Certificate Check blocks performance registry writes for tasks with $\max_i s_i < 1 - \hat{\varepsilon}$.

Failure Mode 3 — Entropy Budget Violation. Training cycles exceeding the TDF entropy budget cause downstream entropy accumulation.
Mitigation: The TDF circuit-breaker halts training and triggers entropy audit when the budget is exceeded.

Failure Mode 4 — Recursive Data Poisoning. Adversarially crafted inputs shift ensemble performance toward a degenerate fixed point.
Mitigation: The 25% human anchor floor and Memory ISS certificate bound corruption propagation.

Failure Mode 5 — Cross-Model Alignment Drift. Model updates cause $\Phi_i$ to drift, increasing $\delta_K$ and degrading $q^*$.
Mitigation: Periodic recalibration on a held-out benchmark corpus maintains the contraction guarantee.

